Date: Mon, 26 Oct 2026 20:45:19 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] oauth: sign a Google account in with a stored refresh token
 (no GOA)

Postcard only got XOAUTH2 credentials from GNOME Online Accounts. This adds a
second source: a refresh token kept in the keyring, exchanged for a short-lived
access token at sign-in via Google's token endpoint, using Thunderbird's
built-in public OAuth client. It lets a Google account imported from another
mail client the user already authorised be used without GOA installed.

- core/net/google_oauth.py: access_token(refresh_token) -> str
- core/secrets.py: OAuthRefresh keyring schema (store/lookup) and credential_for
  returns an XOAUTH2 Credential when a refresh token exists for the account.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>
